WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:14.374
Tootles bragged to the other boys:

2
00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:22.434
"Aha! I have shot the Wendy Bird. Peter will be so proud of me."

3
00:00:22.435 --> 00:00:28.538
"This is no bird," said Slightly. "It's a girl!"

4
00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:32.348
"Now I understand," said Curly.

5
00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:36.564
"Maybe Peter was bringing her here to take care of us."

6
00:00:36.565 --> 00:00:41.412
"And you have killed her!" scolded Nibs.

7
00:00:41.413 --> 00:00:45.992
Tootle's face turned white when he realized his mistake.

8
00:00:45.993 --> 00:00:51.493
He was now afraid of what Peter would say and of how he would be punished.

9
00:00:51.494 --> 00:00:54.522
It was a very tragic moment.

10
00:00:54.523 --> 00:00:58.595
All the boys looked down in deep regret and sorrow.

11
00:00:58.596 --> 00:01:02.610
Just then, they heard a crowing from up above.

12
00:01:02.611 --> 00:01:06.072
This was Peter's usual signal to the boys.

13
00:01:06.073 --> 00:01:10.079
"It's Peter!" the boys cried.

14
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.189
"We must hide her," whispered Nibs.

15
00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:19.650
Nodding, the others crowded around Wendy's body in confusion.

16
00:01:19.651 --> 00:01:24.561
"Greetings, boys," said Peter as he dropped down from the sky.

17
00:01:24.562 --> 00:01:29.543
"I have good news. I've brought a mother to take care of us all."

18
00:01:29.544 --> 00:01:31.943
He looked around at his boys.

19
00:01:31.944 --> 00:01:35.442
There were none of the usual salutes or cheers.

20
00:01:35.443 --> 00:01:42.065
"Why aren't you cheering me?" he asked. "Why so sad?"

21
00:01:42.066 --> 00:01:47.693
The boys stepped aside for Peter to see and then pointed to the body.

22
00:01:47.694 --> 00:01:53.892
"She's dead," said Peter, as he pulled the arrow from Wendy's chest.

23
00:01:53.893 --> 00:01:57.590
"Who did this?"

24
00:01:57.591 --> 00:02:02.345
When Tootles admitted his mistake, Peter raised his arm to hit him.

25
00:02:02.346 --> 00:02:07.939
But a small hand stopped him. Wendy wasn't quite dead yet.

26
00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.415
Even in her weak state, she had protected Tootles.

27
00:02:12.416 --> 00:02:17.623
"She lives!" the boys shouted with joy.

28
00:02:17.624 --> 00:02:22.110
Peter knelt beside her and found the acorn button he had given her.

29
00:02:22.111 --> 00:02:25.055
It was still on a chain around her neck.

30
00:02:25.056 --> 00:02:28.446
It had protected her from the arrow.

31
00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:32.960
"That's the kiss I gave her, and it has saved her life.

32
00:02:32.961 --> 00:02:37.502
I'm such a hero!" cried Peter.

33
00:02:37.503 --> 00:02:43.043
"Hooray!" Now the boys had something to cheer about.

34
00:02:43.044 --> 00:02:45.646
Only Tinker Bell was miserable.

35
00:02:45.647 --> 00:02:49.113
The boys told Peter what she had said to them.

36
00:02:49.114 --> 00:02:53.362
"Tink, I'm ashamed of you!" said Peter.

37
00:02:53.363 --> 00:02:57.619
"Out of my sight! I don't want to see you anymore."

38
00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:03.721
Tinker Bell flew down and landed on Peter's arm. She pleaded with him.

39
00:03:03.722 --> 00:03:08.676
But Wendy, still lying as if dead, raised her arm again.

40
00:03:08.677 --> 00:03:12.919
Feeling a bit sorry for the fairy, Peter gave in.

41
00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:20.080
"Well, maybe I won't banish you forever. But at least for a whole week!"

42
00:03:20.081 --> 00:03:25.023
Even so, Tinker Bell was not the least bit grateful to Wendy.

43
00:03:25.024 --> 00:03:29.005
In fact, she wanted to pinch Wendy even more.

44
00:03:29.006 --> 00:03:33.408
"Let's carry Wendy down to the house," Curly suggested.

45
00:03:33.409 --> 00:03:37.394
"But we shouldn't touch her," said Tootles.

46
00:03:37.395 --> 00:03:41.783
"We might accidentally hurt her even more."

47
00:03:41.784 --> 00:03:47.585
"If she lies here in the open overnight, she'll die," argued Slightly.

48
00:03:47.586 --> 00:03:54.148
"Well then, let's build a temporary little house around her right here," suggested Peter.

49
00:03:54.149 --> 00:03:57.109
"Bring me the best of what each of you have.

50
00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:02.775
You can take it from our house," he ordered in his captain's voice.

51
00:04:02.776 --> 00:04:11.812
Happy to follow Peter's orders again, the boys went about finding soft bedding, firewood, and anything else they could think of.

52
00:04:11.813 --> 00:04:17.712
They went up and down and all around, working hard to make their new mother comfortable.

53
00:04:17.713 --> 00:04:21.759
Suddenly, John and Michael appeared in the sky.

54
00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:29.292
They too were relieved to see Peter again. "Hello, Peter!" they yelled.

55
00:04:29.293 --> 00:04:35.207
"Hello," Peter replied. He had actually forgotten all about them.

56
00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:40.733
Peter was busy measuring Wendy to see how large the new house would need to be.

57
00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:45.143
John and Michael watched the frantic activity around them.

58
00:04:45.144 --> 00:04:51.238
"Is Wendy asleep?" asked John, seeing his sister on the ground.

59
00:04:51.239 --> 00:04:56.242
"Let's wake her up," said Michael. "She can make our dinner."

60
00:04:56.243 --> 00:05:00.680
"Yes, we're hungry!" John shouted.

61
00:05:00.681 --> 00:05:03.413
"Maybe later," said Peter.

62
00:05:03.414 --> 00:05:08.549
"Now you can help the others carry branches to build a house for your sister."

63
00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:14.682
"A house for Wendy?" John exclaimed. "She's only a girl."

64
00:05:14.683 --> 00:05:16.894
"But she's going to be our mother.

65
00:05:16.895 --> 00:05:25.224
We must be respectful and kind," explained Curly.
